# Agent sessions only: share one authenticated connection per host.
#
# Every new connection through Automic Vault's ssh-agent takes ~13s to sign
# (measured 2026-11-18: `ssh picklelab true` 13.6s three times, github.com 14s),
# even though the signature is auto-approved. `just deploy-openclaw` opens ~10
# connections, so it spent ~2 minutes in auth alone. With a ControlMaster the
# first connection pays once and later ssh/scp calls to the same host take ~0s.
#
# Scoped to agent sessions ($CLAUDECODE / $AGENT_SESSION), like agent-relay and
# auth, on purpose:
#   - Own socket directory (~/.ssh/cm-agent, created by sshconfig.sh). A master
#     opened by a human terminal must not be reachable by an agent session, or
#     it could reuse a connection to a host outside the relay allowlist in
#     config/gost/agent-ssh-relay.yml. Humans get no multiplexing from this file.
#   - Multiplexed sessions don't go through the ssh-agent, so `av history` shows
#     one entry per master instead of one per use.
# The path must stay short: a unix socket path is limited to ~104 bytes, and %C
# is a 40-character hash.
#
# `ssh -O exit <host>` (with the same ControlPath) closes a master early. If a
# connection acts stuck, `rm ~/.ssh/cm-agent/*`.
Match exec "test -n \"$CLAUDECODE$AGENT_SESSION\""
  ControlMaster auto
  ControlPath ~/.ssh/cm-agent/%C
  ControlPersist 5m
